        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: respect configured Crabbox provider for agent tests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's agent-testing guidance hardcoded Blacksmith Testbox for ordinary trusted validation. That caused agents to override an existing explicit Crabbox choice such as `CRABBOX_PROVIDER=local-container`, even though the wrapper already supports that environment override before the repository's Blacksmith default.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe testing and Crabbox skills now tell trusted agent workflows to omit `--provider` unless a specific proof or safety route requires one. This preserves the existing wrapper contract:\n\n1. an explicitly requested/command-line provider;\n2. `CRABBOX_PROVIDER`;\n3. the repository `.crabbox.yaml` default (`blacksmith-testbox`).\n\nThe skills also distinguish a Crabbox-managed `local-container` run from direct host testing and require provider attribution from wrapper/config output instead of inferring AWS from the shared `cbx_...` lease prefix.\n\nClawSweeper correctly identified that `crabbox config show --json` does not create a user-config preference above repository config. The PR was narrowed accordingly: it no longer changes `scripts/crabbox-wrapper.mjs`, adds no merged-config precedence contract, and adds no new fail-closed startup behavior.\n\nAI-assisted: this change was agent-tested with Claude through `acpx`, reviewed with Codex autoreview, and revised in response to ClawSweeper.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDevelopers who explicitly set `CRABBOX_PROVIDER` can run ordinary trusted agent validation on that backend without agents forcing Blacksmith Testbox. Developers without an explicit override continue to use the repository's Blacksmith Testbox default.\n\nA configured local container still executes tests inside a Crabbox-managed Docker lease; it does not silently downgrade to host-local execution. Remote, cross-platform, untrusted-source, and Testbox-specific proof requirements continue to select their required backend explicitly.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blind `acpx claude` validation independently resolved the inherited `CRABBOX_PROVIDER=local-container`; the prompt did not name the expected provider.\n- The first agent attempt exposed a guidance defect by running the focused test directly on the host. That result was rejected, and the skills were clarified to require wrapper-managed Docker execution for `local-container`.\n- Post-fix Claude runs correctly provisioned local-container Docker leases, ran the focused wrapper suite inside the containers, and cleaned up their leases.\n- Final post-rebase proof:\n  - base: `upstream/main` at `161525d43c4c0157a8fd4feceb2bf96cb4db5900`;\n  - provider/runtime: `provider=local-container`, `runtime=docker`, Crabbox `0.37.1`;\n  - lease: `cbx_29a3dd41d47d` / `brisk-crab-d2c5`, explicitly deleted after the run;\n  - command: `node scripts/crabbox-wrapper.mjs run --id cbx_29a3dd41d47d --timing-json -- corepack pnpm test test/scripts/crabbox-wrapper.test.ts --reporter=default`;\n  - result: 1 test file passed; 192/192 tests passed.\n- Final diff relative to `upstream/main`: two skill files only; zero wrapper/test code diff.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main --stream-engine-output` — clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
        "branch": "feature/respect-crabbox-provider-preference",
